 "purpose": "The colour themes: screens ask for a ROLE (good, wrong, accent ...), never a colour; this file maps roles to curses attributes per theme, and builds avatar pixel colour pairs.",
 "details": "Themes: standard, two colour-blind themes (Okabe-Ito colours: red-green and blue-yellow), high contrast and no colour (only bold, underline, reverse, also for terminals without colours). Right and wrong always also have a symbol on screen. Roles include the sentence-part colours (z_pv ... z_bwb, like highlighter pens, with the abbreviation always shown too) and the panel-screen roles (vraag, band, invulcursor, rand, rand_focus). Colours are written by name (8 colours) or (number for 256 colours, name for 8). maak() builds {role: attribute}; pixel() and rol_pixel() create colour pairs for half-block pixels lazily from pair number 32. No colour code elsewhere in the program (a test guards it).",
 "module_docstring": "Kleurenthema's. Schermen vragen een ROL (\"goed\", \"fout\", \"accent\" …), nooit een kleur.",
